Appendix E: Proposed Certification Standards and Ethical Code

E.1 Certification Body

A professional society for AI Workforce Governance (to be established) would maintain a certification scheme requiring:

· Successful completion of an accredited training program covering all competencies in Appendix B at the specified levels.
· A cumulative portfolio of at least three governed deployments (simulated or live) demonstrating maintained alignment over time and across distributional shifts.
· Passing an examination covering formal modeling, reward design, forensic analysis, and ethical governance.

E.2 Ethical Code of Practice

1. Dual Loyalty: The AI Workforce Designer’s primary loyalty is to the ultimate organizational mission and societal welfare, not to any single proxy metric or stakeholder demand.
2. Transparency: All proxy objectives, their known limitations, and their Goodhart Numbers shall be documented and disclosed to relevant governance bodies.
3. Non-Abandonment of Oversight: No synthetic workforce shall be deployed without a continuously operational Institutional Immune System; fully automated governance without a bounded human channel is prohibited.
4. Adversarial Integrity: Designers shall not interfere with the independence of auditors, nor penalize agents that expose flaws in the incentive system during sanctioned red-teaming.
5. Ongoing Competency: Practitioners shall maintain their skills through periodic re-certification, reflecting the evolving nature of both agent capabilities and adversarial threats.



